{"name":"Golden Hour","hex":"#f1b457","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"golden hour","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The first sixty minutes after sustaining major traumatic injury, during which there is the highest likelihood that prompt medical treatment will prevent death.","A period shortly after sunrise or before sunset, during which daylight is redder and softer than when the Sun is higher in the sky."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/golden_hour"}],"entries":[{"title":"Golden hour (medicine)","blocks":[{"text":"In emergency medicine, the golden hour is the period of time immediately after a traumatic injury during which there is the highest likelihood that prompt medical and surgical treatment will prevent death. While initially defined as an hour, the exact time period depends on the nature of the injury and can be more than or less than this duration. It is well established that the person's chances of survival are greatest if they receive care within a short period of time after a severe injury; however, there is no evidence to suggest that survival rates drop off after 60 minutes. Some have come to use the term to refer to the core principle of rapid intervention in trauma cases, rather than the narrow meaning of a critical one-hour time period."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Golden_hour_graph.png/330px-Golden_hour_graph.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golden_hour_(medicine)","wikidata":"Q2708761"},{"title":"Golden hour (photography)","blocks":[{"text":"In photography, the golden hour is the period of daytime shortly after sunrise or before sunset, during which daylight is redder and softer than when the sun is higher in the sky."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Newbury_Racecourse_Road.jpg/330px-Newbury_Racecourse_Road.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golden_hour_(photography)","wikidata":"Q3238843"},{"title":"Golden Hour (Kacey Musgraves album)","blocks":[{"text":"Golden Hour is the fourth studio album by American country music singer and songwriter Kacey Musgraves, released on March 30, 2018, through MCA Nashville. Musgraves co-wrote all 13 tracks and co-produced the album with Daniel Tashian and Ian Fitchuk. A country pop record, Golden Hour also contains elements of disco, electropop, electronica, and yacht rock."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/65/Kacey_Musgraves_-_Golden_Hour.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golden_Hour_(Kacey_Musgraves_album)","wikidata":"Q51155613"},{"title":"Hour","blocks":[{"text":"An hour is a unit of time historically reckoned as 1⁄24 of a day and defined contemporarily as exactly 3,600 seconds. There are 60 minutes in an hour, and 24 hours in a day."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/AnalogClockAnimation1_2hands_1h_in_6sec.gif/330px-AnalogClockAnimation1_2hands_1h_in_6sec.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hour","wikidata":"Q25235"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/PlanckianLocus.png/500px-PlanckianLocus.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/PlanckianLocus.png/1280px-PlanckianLocus.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/PlanckianLocus.png/500px-PlanckianLocus.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The color temperature of daylight varies with the time of day. It tends to be around 2,000 K shortly after sunrise or before sunset, around 3,500 K during \"golden hour\", and around 5,500 K at midday. The color temperature can also change significantly with altitude, latitude, season, and weather conditions.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APlanckianLocus.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/20240920_53rd_Street_Hyde_Park_Chicago_near_equinox_stacked_rotated_and_recropped_4x3.jpg/500px-20240920_53rd_Street_Hyde_Park_Chicago_near_equinox_stacked_rotated_and_recropped_4x3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/20240920_53rd_Street_Hyde_Park_Chicago_near_equinox_stacked_rotated_and_recropped_4x3.jpg/1280px-20240920_53rd_Street_Hyde_Park_Chicago_near_equinox_stacked_rotated_and_recropped_4x3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/20240920_53rd_Street_Hyde_Park_Chicago_near_equinox_stacked_rotated_and_recropped_4x3.jpg/500px-20240920_53rd_Street_Hyde_Park_Chicago_near_equinox_stacked_rotated_and_recropped_4x3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Near the equinoxes in Chicago the sunsets occur in the middle of east-west streets (an event known as Chicagohenge), creating intriguing golden hour photography opportunities like this diffraction spike in an urban canyon. Similar phenomena (such as Manhattanhenge) occur in other parts of the world at various times of the year.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A20240920_53rd_Street_Hyde_Park_Chicago_near_equinox_stacked_rotated_and_recropped_4x3.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Bangkok_skytrain_sunset.jpg/500px-Bangkok_skytrain_sunset.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Bangkok_skytrain_sunset.jpg/960px-Ba